1://! Experimental asynchronous DSA bytes codec for tonic.
2://!
3://! This crate exercises tonic's owned encode `Future` path with an explicit
4://! in-flight Intel DSA copy. The encoder keeps ordinary CPU encoding as the
5://! default when no work queue is configured. When DSA is enabled, encoding
6://! returns an owned operation that submits a memmove descriptor, yields
7://! `Poll::Pending`, and finishes the gRPC frame after the descriptor completion
8://! record reaches a terminal status.
9://!
10://! The implementation transfers owned encode storage into per-message encode
11://! state before polling. Pending DSA work keeps that storage and its direct-DMA
12://! pointer inside the encode operation until completion.
